      <!-- HERO SECTION -->
      <div class="hero" id="overview">
        <div class="hero-content">
          <h2>Start Planning Your Future Today</h2>
          <p>Welcome! Preparing for your dream profession begins right now in
            middle school. Explore detailed, step-by-step educational roadmaps
            tailored for Class 8 students in Bangladesh covering secondary
            school, college, university admission requirements, and professional
            certifications.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-img"> <img src="file:///C:/Users/rrahm/OneDrive/Desktop/ICT/Website/Baliadanga1/professions.jpg"
            alt="Careers" title="Professions" style="width: 445px; height: 243px;"></div>
      </div>
      <!-- QUICK LINKS SECTION -->
      <div class="quick-links">
        <h3>Explore Career Streams</h3>
        <div class="link-grid"> <a href="#doctor" class="link-card">🩺 Medical
            Doctor (MBBS)</a> <a href="#engineer" class="link-card">⚙️ Engineer
            (B.Sc. / Diploma)</a> <a href="#nurse" class="link-card">🏥
            Registered Nurse</a> <a href="#teacher" class="link-card">📚
            Educator / Teacher</a> <a href="#army" class="link-card">🎖️
            Bangladesh Army Officer</a> </div>
      </div>
      <!-- DOCTOR PATH -->
      <div class="section" id="doctor">
        <h2>1. Medical Doctor (MBBS)</h2>
        <p><strong>Overview:</strong> Becoming a medical doctor in Bangladesh
          requires a structured academic roadmap from school through university
          and hospital training [<a href="#ref-17">17</a>, <a href="#ref-18">18</a>].</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Class 8 to SSC (Phase 1):</strong> Focus heavily on
            General Science, Mathematics, and English [<a href="#ref-15">15</a>].
            Build deep conceptual understanding rather than memorizing answers [<a
              href="#ref-15">15</a>]. Plan to select the Science Group in Class
            9, ensuring you take Biology, Chemistry, and Physics [<a href="#ref-15">15</a>].</li>
          <li><strong>SSC Stage (Phase 2):</strong> Aim for a GPA of 5.0 (or the
            highest possible score) in your SSC exams [<a href="#ref-12">12</a>,
            <a href="#ref-19">19</a>]. Pay extra attention to Biology and
            Chemistry as the foundation for medical tests [<a href="#ref-12">12</a>].
            Meet the BMDC combined high GPA requirements across SSC and HSC [<a
              href="#ref-17">17</a>, <a href="#ref-19">19</a>].</li>
          <li><strong>HSC Stage (Phase 3):</strong> Enroll in the Science stream
            with mandatory Physics, Chemistry, and Biology [<a href="#ref-17">17</a>].
            Target a strong combined GPA (around 8.50+ for general applicants)
            and at least 3.50 in Biology [<a href="#ref-19">19</a>]. Join a
            dedicated medical admission coaching program during your 2nd year or
            right after HSC [<a href="#ref-17">17</a>].</li>
          <li><strong>Admission &amp; MBBS (Phase 4):</strong> Sit for the
            centralized Medical Admission Test conducted by the DGHS evaluating
            Biology, Chemistry, Physics, and English [<a href="#ref-12">12</a>,
            <a href="#ref-17">17</a>]. If selected, complete the 5-year MBBS
            academic and clinical course, moving from basic medical sciences
            into clinical wards [<a href="#ref-17">17</a>, <a href="#ref-20">20</a>,
            <a href="#ref-21">21</a>].</li>
          <li><strong>Internship &amp; Registration (Phase 5):</strong> Complete
            a 1-year mandatory rotator internship at a recognized hospital and
            register with the BMDC to legally practice as a physician [<a href="#ref-17">17</a>,
            <a href="#ref-20">20</a>].</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <!-- ENGINEER PATH -->
      <div class="section" id="engineer">
        <h2>2. Engineer (B.Sc. / Diploma)</h2>
        <p><strong>Overview:</strong> Becoming an engineer requires building a
          strong foundation in science and mathematics starting from Class 8 [<a
            href="#ref-15">15</a>, <a href="#ref-22">22</a>].</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Class 8 to SSC (Phase 1):</strong> Master NCTB textbooks
            for Mathematics and General Science, focusing on algebra, geometry,
            and basic physical laws [<a href="#ref-15">15</a>, <a href="#ref-12">12</a>].
            Select the Science Group in Class 9 with Higher Mathematics and
            Physics as mandatory stepping stones, aiming for a GPA 5.00 in SSC [<a
              href="#ref-15">15</a>, <a href="#ref-12">12</a>].</li>
          <li><strong>HSC Level (Phase 2):</strong> Get admitted to a reputed
            college with a strong Science faculty (Physics, Chemistry, Higher
            Math) and score a GPA 5.00 in HSC [<a href="#ref-15">15</a>]. Clear
            competitive university admission tests for public universities
            (BUET, CUET, KUET, RUET) or top private options (AUST, BRACU, IUT,
            NSU), or opt for a 4-year Diploma via BTEB [<a href="#ref-12">12</a>,
            <a href="#ref-23">23</a>].</li>
          <li><strong>Undergraduate Degree (Phase 3):</strong> Enroll in a
            4-year B.Sc. in Engineering degree choosing a discipline like CSE,
            EEE, or Civil Engineering [<a href="#ref-12">12</a>, <a href="#ref-15">15</a>].
            Work on practical lab projects, coding, and CAD drafting [<a href="#ref-12">12</a>,
            <a href="#ref-24">24</a>].</li>
          <li><strong>Professional Practice:</strong> Complete internships
            during your graduation and register with the Institution of
            Engineers, Bangladesh (IEB) [<a href="#ref-2">2</a>, <a href="#ref-24">24</a>].</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <!-- NURSE PATH -->
      <div class="section" id="nurse">
        <h2>3. Registered Nurse</h2>
        <p><strong>Overview:</strong> To become a registered nurse in
          Bangladesh, you must complete secondary and higher secondary education
          and pass the central BNMC admission test [<a href="#ref-1">1</a>, <a
            href="#ref-7">7</a>, <a href="#ref-10">10</a>].</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Class 8 to SSC:</strong> Continue your school studies
            focusing heavily on General Science and English, aiming for an SSC
            GPA of at least 3.00 to 3.50+ [<a href="#ref-1">1</a>, <a href="#ref-3">3</a>,
            <a href="#ref-5">5</a>].</li>
          <li><strong>HSC Stage:</strong> Choose the Science Group in class 9
            and continue through HSC with Biology as a core subject (mandatory
            for B.Sc.) [<a href="#ref-2">2</a>, <a href="#ref-4">4</a>].
            Maintain a minimum HSC GPA of 3.00, with a combined SSC and HSC
            total GPA of at least 7.00 for B.Sc. (or 6.00 for the 3-year
            Diploma) [<a href="#ref-2">2</a>, <a href="#ref-5">5</a>].</li>
          <li><strong>Choose Your Program:</strong> Apply for either the 4-year
            B.Sc. in Nursing (Basic) requiring Science with Biology and a 7.00
            total GPA, or the 3-year Diploma in Nursing Science and Midwifery
            requiring a total GPA of 6.00 in any group [<a href="#ref-4">4</a>,
            <a href="#ref-7">7</a>, <a href="#ref-25">25</a>].</li>
          <li><strong>Admission &amp; Licensing:</strong> Fill out online
            applications through the government portal and clear the centralized
            MCQ test covering Bangla, English, Math, General Science, and GK [<a
              href="#ref-3">3</a>, <a href="#ref-8">8</a>, <a href="#ref-9">9</a>].
            Complete your clinical internship and clear the BNMC Comprehensive
            Licensing Exam for official registration [<a href="#ref-6">6</a>, <a
              href="#ref-10">10</a>, <a href="#ref-26">26</a>].</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <!-- TEACHER PATH -->
      <div class="section" id="teacher">
        <h2>4. Educator / Teacher</h2>
        <p><strong>Overview:</strong> To become a teacher in Bangladesh, you
          must complete secondary and higher secondary education, earn a
          bachelor’s degree, and obtain specific teaching certifications [<a href="#ref-11">11</a>,
          <a href="#ref-27">27</a>].</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>High School &amp; SSC (Classes 8–10):</strong> Build a
            strong foundation in Mathematics, English, Bangla, and General
            Science, maintaining a high GPA and avoiding grade drops to meet
            strict recruitment criteria [<a href="#ref-12">12</a>, <a href="#ref-2">2</a>].
            Practice clear communication and patience [<a href="#ref-13">13</a>].</li>
          <li><strong>Higher Secondary (Classes 11–12):</strong> Pick Science,
            Arts/Humanities, or Commerce based on the subject you want to teach,
            and achieve a strong HSC GPA [<a href="#ref-11">11</a>, <a href="#ref-13">13</a>].</li>
          <li><strong>University &amp; Bachelor’s Degree:</strong> Enroll in a
            public or private university for a 3 or 4-year Honours degree in
            your preferred subject [<a href="#ref-13">13</a>, <a href="#ref-27">27</a>].
            Pursue a B.Ed. or M.Ed. to gain professional training in child
            psychology, lesson planning, and modern teaching methods [<a href="#ref-11">11</a>,
            <a href="#ref-14">14</a>].</li>
          <li><strong>Certification &amp; Recruitment:</strong> Register and
            pass the NTRCA exams for non-government schools [<a href="#ref-11">11</a>,
            <a href="#ref-27">27</a>], apply through DPE for government primary
            assistant teacher tests [<a href="#ref-27">27</a>], or compete in
            the BPSC BCS (General Education) exams for government colleges [<a href="#ref-11">11</a>,
            <a href="#ref-14">14</a>].</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <!-- ARMY OFFICER PATH -->
      <div class="section" id="army">
        <h2>5. Bangladesh Army Officer</h2>
        <p><strong>Overview:</strong> To become an officer or soldier in the
          Bangladesh Army, you need to focus on school studies, physical
          fitness, and general knowledge starting from Class 8 [<a href="#ref-28">28</a>,
          <a href="#ref-29">29</a>].</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Education Plan (Class 8 to HSC):</strong> Focus heavily on
            Mathematics, English, Bangla, and General Science, aiming for a GPA
            of 5.00 in SSC [<a href="#ref-28">28</a>, <a href="#ref-14">14</a>].
            Consider residential Cadet Colleges for specialized training [<a href="#ref-14">14</a>].
            Maintain excellence (GPA 4.5 to 5.00) in Science, Arts, or Commerce
            at the HSC level [<a href="#ref-28">28</a>, <a href="#ref-29">29</a>].</li>
          <li><strong>Officer Eligibility (BMA Long Course):</strong> Meet the
            age requirement (16 years 6 months to 21 years), remain unmarried,
            satisfy high minimum GPA standards in SSC and HSC, and meet physical
            standards like minimum height (approx. 5 feet 4 inches) [<a href="#ref-28">28</a>,
            <a href="#ref-29">29</a>].</li>
          <li><strong>Alternative Entry:</strong> Apply directly as a soldier
            (recruit) via national newspaper notices and Teletalk SMS right
            after passing SSC [<a href="#ref-28">28</a>, <a href="#ref-15">15</a>].</li>
          <li><strong>Key Skill Development:</strong> Build fluent English
            communication for the ISSB, maintain stamina through regular
            physical training, and study daily current affairs and IQ tests [<a
              href="#ref-15">15</a>, <a href="#ref-28">28</a>].</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
